[{"id":1795025155832,"front":"A value <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>X</mi>\n</math></span> comes from one of two groups, each chosen with probability <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span>.<ul><li>Group 0: mean <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span>, variance <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n</math></span>.</li><li>Group 1: mean <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>4</mn>\n</math></span>, variance <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n</math></span>.</li></ul>Let <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>G</mi>\n</math></span> denote the chosen group label.<b>Find the variance of <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>X</mi>\n</math></span> across both groups.</b><p>Show your calculation from <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>Var</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n</math></span>. Explain how differences within each group and between the group means contribute to the answer.</p>","back":"<span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>∣</mo>\n  <mi>G</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mi>Var</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo>∣</mo>\n  <mi>G</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo>∣</mo>\n  <mi>G</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n</math></span>, taking expectations and subtracting <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n</math></span> gives <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>Var</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mi>Var</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo>∣</mo>\n  <mi>G</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <mi>Var</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo>∣</mo>\n  <mi>G</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span> Here the within-group contribution is <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n</math></span>; the between-group contribution is <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mfrac>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n    </mfrac>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mfrac>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n    </mfrac>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>4</mn>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>4</mn>\n</math></span>. Thus <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>Var</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>5</mn>\n</math></span>. Averaging the two conditional variances misses the variation between group centers."},{"id":1795025155878,"front":"The random variable <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>X</mi>\n</math></span> has density <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>f</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>e</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n      <mi>x</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </msup>\n</math></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>x</mi>\n  <mo>≥</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span> otherwise.<p><b>Find its moment generating function <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>M</mi>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span>.</b> Start from the defining expectation and state which real values of <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>t</mi>\n</math></span> give a finite result.</p><p>Then use the derivatives of <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>M</mi>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span> to calculate the mean and variance of <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>X</mi>\n</math></span>.</p>","back":"By definition, <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>M</mi>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>e</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>t</mi>\n      <mi>X</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </msup>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <msubsup>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∫</mo>\n    <mn>0</mn>\n    <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi>\n  </msubsup>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>e</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mi>t</mi>\n      <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n      <mi>x</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </msup>\n  <mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi>d</mi>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n    <mrow>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mi>t</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </mfrac>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo>&lt;</mo>\n  <mn>2.</mn>\n</math></span> At <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span> the integrand is constant and the integral diverges; for <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo>&gt;</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span> it grows. On a neighborhood of zero the MGF is finite and can be differentiated for moments: <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msubsup>\n    <mi>M</mi>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi data-mjx-alternate=\"1\">′</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </msubsup>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msubsup>\n    <mi>M</mi>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi data-mjx-alternate=\"1\">′</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </msubsup>\n  <mi data-mjx-alternate=\"1\">′</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span>. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>Var</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>4</mn>\n</math></span>. The second derivative gives the second raw moment, not the variance directly."},{"id":1795025155936,"front":"You take three independent measurements <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n    <mn>3</mn>\n  </msub>\n</math></span> from a Normal distribution with mean <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>μ</mi>\n</math></span> and variance <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msup>\n    <mi>σ</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>&gt;</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span>. Their sample mean and sample variance are <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mover>\n      <mi>X</mi>\n      <mo stretchy=\"false\">¯</mo>\n    </mover>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mrow>\n      <msub>\n        <mi>X</mi>\n        <mn>1</mn>\n      </msub>\n      <mo>+</mo>\n      <msub>\n        <mi>X</mi>\n        <mn>2</mn>\n      </msub>\n      <mo>+</mo>\n      <msub>\n        <mi>X</mi>\n        <mn>3</mn>\n      </msub>\n    </mrow>\n    <mn>3</mn>\n  </mfrac>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>S</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </mfrac>\n  <munderover>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∑</mo>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>i</mi>\n      <mo>=</mo>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n    </mrow>\n    <mn>3</mn>\n  </munderover>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>X</mi>\n    <mi>i</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mover>\n      <mi>X</mi>\n      <mo stretchy=\"false\">¯</mo>\n    </mover>\n  </mrow>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span><b>What distribution does <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>T</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <msqrt>\n    <mn>3</mn>\n  </msqrt>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mover>\n      <mi>X</mi>\n      <mo stretchy=\"false\">¯</mo>\n    </mover>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mi>μ</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mi>S</mi>\n</math></span> have?</b><p>Explain the degrees of freedom and state which quantities must be independent for your argument. Explain how the answer changes if the denominator is the true standard deviation <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>σ</mi>\n</math></span> instead of the sample standard deviation <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>S</mi>\n</math></span>.</p>","back":"Write <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>Z</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mrow>\n      <msqrt>\n        <mn>3</mn>\n      </msqrt>\n      <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n      <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n        <mover>\n          <mi>X</mi>\n          <mo stretchy=\"false\">¯</mo>\n        </mover>\n      </mrow>\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mi>μ</mi>\n      <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    </mrow>\n    <mi>σ</mi>\n  </mfrac>\n  <mo>∼</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mi data-mjx-variant=\"-tex-calligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">N</mi>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi>V</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mrow>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n      <msup>\n        <mi>S</mi>\n        <mn>2</mn>\n      </msup>\n    </mrow>\n    <msup>\n      <mi>σ</mi>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n    </msup>\n  </mfrac>\n  <mo>∼</mo>\n  <msubsup>\n    <mi>χ</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msubsup>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span> For an independent Gaussian sample, <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mover>\n      <mi>X</mi>\n      <mo stretchy=\"false\">¯</mo>\n    </mover>\n  </mrow>\n</math></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msup>\n    <mi>S</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n</math></span> are independent, so <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>Z</mi>\n</math></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>V</mi>\n</math></span> are independent. Hence <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>T</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mi>Z</mi>\n    <msqrt>\n      <mi>V</mi>\n      <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n        <mo>/</mo>\n      </mrow>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n    </msqrt>\n  </mfrac>\n  <mo>∼</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>t</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span> The three residuals sum to zero, leaving a two-dimensional residual subspace. Replacing <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>S</mi>\n</math></span> by the fixed <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>σ</mi>\n</math></span> leaves <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>Z</mi>\n</math></span>, which is standard Normal. The random estimate in the denominator produces the heavier tails. Gaussianity matters for the exact chi-squared and independence claims."},{"id":1795025156025,"front":"A student applies L’Hôpital’s rule as follows: <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <munder>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\" movablelimits=\"true\">lim</mo>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>x</mi>\n      <mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo>\n      <mn>0</mn>\n    </mrow>\n  </munder>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mrow>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n      <mo>+</mo>\n      <mi>sin</mi>\n      <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo>\n      <mi>x</mi>\n    </mrow>\n    <mrow>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n      <mo>+</mo>\n      <mi>x</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </mfrac>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <munder>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\" movablelimits=\"true\">lim</mo>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>x</mi>\n      <mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo>\n      <mn>0</mn>\n    </mrow>\n  </munder>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mrow>\n      <mi>cos</mi>\n      <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo>\n      <mi>x</mi>\n    </mrow>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </mfrac>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1.</mn>\n</math></span><b>Explain why this use of L’Hôpital’s rule is invalid, and find the correct limit.</b><p>Then replace the constants <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n</math></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span> in the original fraction so that the rule does apply. Leave <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>sin</mi>\n  <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n</math></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>x</mi>\n</math></span>, and the limit point unchanged.</p>","back":"The original ratio has limit <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span> by continuity. It is neither a <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span> nor an infinite-over-infinite indeterminate form, so L Hopital does not apply. A repair is <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>sin</mi>\n  <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n</math></span>: both numerator and denominator approach zero, the denominator derivative is nonzero, and the derivative ratio <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>cos</mi>\n  <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n</math></span> approaches <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n</math></span>. Differentiation discards additive constants. Those constants determine the original finite nonzero ratio and cannot be discarded there."},{"id":1795025156077,"front":"Let <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>s</mi>\n</math></span> be a fixed positive real number.<p><b>Use integration by parts to calculate</b> <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>I</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>s</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <msubsup>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∫</mo>\n    <mn>0</mn>\n    <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi>\n  </msubsup>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>t</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>e</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mi>s</mi>\n      <mi>t</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </msup>\n  <mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi>d</mi>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span>Keep <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>s</mi>\n</math></span> in your answer. Show what happens to the boundary terms at <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span> and as <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo>\n  <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi>\n</math></span>. Then evaluate your formula at <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>s</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>3</mn>\n</math></span>.</p>","back":"The boundary terms vanish because <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msup>\n    <mi>t</mi>\n    <mi>k</mi>\n  </msup>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>e</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mi>s</mi>\n      <mi>t</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </msup>\n  <mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo>\n  <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi>\n</math></span> for fixed <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>s</mi>\n  <mo>&gt;</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span>, and the powers vanish at zero. Twice integrating by parts gives <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>I</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>s</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n    <mi>s</mi>\n  </mfrac>\n  <msubsup>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∫</mo>\n    <mn>0</mn>\n    <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi>\n  </msubsup>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>e</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mi>s</mi>\n      <mi>t</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </msup>\n  <mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi>d</mi>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n    <msup>\n      <mi>s</mi>\n      <mn>2</mn>\n    </msup>\n  </mfrac>\n  <msubsup>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∫</mo>\n    <mn>0</mn>\n    <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi>\n  </msubsup>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>e</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mi>s</mi>\n      <mi>t</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </msup>\n  <mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi>d</mi>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mfrac>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n    <msup>\n      <mi>s</mi>\n      <mn>3</mn>\n    </msup>\n  </mfrac>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span> Thus <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>I</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>3</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>27</mn>\n</math></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>s</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n</math></span>, the value is <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo>!</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Γ</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>3</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span>, not <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Γ</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span>. This is an exact convergent integral, not an undamped oscillatory Fourier integral."},{"id":1795025156177,"front":"Let <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\">\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo>\n    <mtable columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"4pt\">\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>2</mn>\n        </mtd>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>0</mn>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>0</mn>\n        </mtd>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>5</mn>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n    </mtable>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\">\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo>\n    <mtable columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"4pt\">\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>1</mn>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>1</mn>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n    </mtable>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span><b>Find constants <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mn>0</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </msub>\n</math></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mn>0</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mi>I</mi>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n    </mrow>\n  </msup>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n</math></span>.</b><p>Here <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>I</mi>\n</math></span> is the identity matrix. Show how each coordinate gives an equation for the constants.</p><p>Write your result as <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>p</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n</math></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>p</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mn>0</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n</math></span>. Explain why it lies in the Krylov space <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi data-mjx-variant=\"-tex-calligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">K</mi>\n    </mrow>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mi>span</mi>\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo>\n</math></span>, the set of linear combinations of <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>b</mi>\n</math></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n</math></span>.</p>","back":"The two conditions are <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>p</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>p</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>5</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>5</mn>\n</math></span>. Thus <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>3</mn>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mn>3</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>10</mn>\n</math></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>10</mn>\n</math></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mn>0</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>7</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>10</mn>\n</math></span>. Consequently <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>p</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mfrac>\n      <mn>7</mn>\n      <mn>10</mn>\n    </mfrac>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mfrac>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n      <mn>10</mn>\n    </mfrac>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>5</mn>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mi>T</mi>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n</math></span> whose image under <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>A</mi>\n</math></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>b</mi>\n</math></span>. It belongs to <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi data-mjx-variant=\"-tex-calligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">K</mi>\n    </mrow>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mi>span</mi>\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo>\n</math></span> because it is explicitly a linear combination of those generating vectors. Interpolating the inverse at both eigenvalues makes one polynomial handle both components."},{"id":1795025156277,"front":"The events <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mo>…</mo>\n</math></span> grow: <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>⊆</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>n</mi>\n      <mo>+</mo>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n    </mrow>\n  </msub>\n</math></span> for every <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>n</mi>\n</math></span>. Let <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <munderover>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">⋃</mo>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>n</mi>\n      <mo>=</mo>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n    </mrow>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </munderover>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </msub>\n</math></span>, the event that at least one of them occurs.<p><b>Use countable additivity to prove <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <munder>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\" movablelimits=\"true\">lim</mo>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>n</mi>\n      <mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo>\n      <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi>\n    </mrow>\n  </munder>\n  <mi>P</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mi>P</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span>.</b></p><p>Check the direction of the assumption: if <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>X</mi>\n</math></span> is uniform on <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n</math></span>, do the events <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo>\n  <mi>X</mi>\n  <mo>∈</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mi>n</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo>\n</math></span> grow or shrink as <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>n</mi>\n</math></span> increases? Which values of <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>X</mi>\n</math></span> remain in every one of these events?</p>","back":"Define disjoint increments <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>B</mi>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mn>1</mn>\n  </msub>\n</math></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>B</mi>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>∖</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>n</mi>\n      <mo>−</mo>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n    </mrow>\n  </msub>\n</math></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>n</mi>\n  <mo>≥</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span>. Then <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <munderover>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">⋃</mo>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>k</mi>\n      <mo>=</mo>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n    </mrow>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </munderover>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>B</mi>\n    <mi>k</mi>\n  </msub>\n</math></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <munder>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">⋃</mo>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>k</mi>\n      <mo>≥</mo>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n    </mrow>\n  </munder>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>B</mi>\n    <mi>k</mi>\n  </msub>\n</math></span>. Countable additivity gives <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>P</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <munder>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∑</mo>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>k</mi>\n      <mo>≥</mo>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n    </mrow>\n  </munder>\n  <mi>P</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>B</mi>\n    <mi>k</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <munder>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\" movablelimits=\"true\">lim</mo>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </munder>\n  <munderover>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∑</mo>\n    <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n      <mi>k</mi>\n      <mo>=</mo>\n      <mn>1</mn>\n    </mrow>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </munderover>\n  <mi>P</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>B</mi>\n    <mi>k</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <munder>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\" movablelimits=\"true\">lim</mo>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </munder>\n  <mi>P</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span> The intervals <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mi>n</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span> decrease rather than increase. Their intersection is <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo>\n</math></span>, whose uniform probability is zero, consistent with <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>P</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>A</mi>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mi>n</mi>\n  <mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></span>. The set limit is not <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span>."},{"id":1795025156328,"front":"The function <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>F</mi>\n</math></span> takes two inputs and returns a vector: <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>F</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>y</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\">\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo>\n    <mtable columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"4pt\">\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <mi>x</mi>\n          <mi>y</mi>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <msup>\n            <mi>x</mi>\n            <mn>2</mn>\n          </msup>\n          <mo>+</mo>\n          <mi>y</mi>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n    </mtable>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span>Start at <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>y</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span>. Make a small change: add <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>ε</mi>\n</math></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>x</mi>\n</math></span> and subtract <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mi>ε</mi>\n</math></span> from <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>y</mi>\n</math></span>.<p><b>Compare the change predicted by the Jacobian with the exact change in <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>F</mi>\n</math></span>.</b></p><p>Calculate the Jacobian at <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span>, multiply it by the displacement vector <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>h</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>ε</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mi>ε</mi>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mi>T</mi>\n  </msup>\n</math></span>, and compare that vector with <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>F</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <mi>ε</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mi>ε</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mi>F</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span>. State which terms the approximation leaves out.</p>","back":"<span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>J</mi>\n    <mi>F</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>y</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\">\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo>\n    <mtable columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"4pt\">\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <mi>y</mi>\n        </mtd>\n        <mtd>\n          <mi>x</mi>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>2</mn>\n          <mi>x</mi>\n        </mtd>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>1</mn>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n    </mtable>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\">\n    <mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <msub>\n    <mi>J</mi>\n    <mi>F</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\">\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo>\n    <mtable columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"4pt\">\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>2</mn>\n        </mtd>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>1</mn>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n      <mtr>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>2</mn>\n        </mtd>\n        <mtd>\n          <mn>1</mn>\n        </mtd>\n      </mtr>\n    </mtable>\n    <mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span> Hence <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>J</mi>\n    <mi>F</mi>\n  </msub>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mi>h</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mi>T</mi>\n  </msup>\n</math></span>: both first-order terms cancel in this direction. Direct substitution gives <span class=\"display-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n  <mi>F</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <mi>ε</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mi>ε</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mi>F</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>ε</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>ε</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <msup>\n    <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n    <mi>T</mi>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>.</mo>\n</math></span> The change is generally nonzero, but is second order. A zero directional derivative means no first-order change, not that the function stays exactly constant along the line."},{"id":1795025156378,"front":"Start with three different objects in the order <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mi>A</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>B</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>C</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</math></span>. Shuffle them in three steps:<ol><li>Swap position <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n</math></span> with a randomly chosen position.</li><li>Swap position <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>2</mn>\n</math></span> with a randomly chosen position.</li><li>Swap position <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>3</mn>\n</math></span> with a randomly chosen position.</li></ol>Each time, choose independently from positions <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>3</mn>\n</math></span>, with equal probabilities. Swapping a position with itself is allowed.<p><b>Does this give each of the six possible final orders probability <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>6</mn>\n</math></span>?</b> Justify your answer by counting the equally likely sequences of random choices.</p><p>How should the allowed positions for the random choice <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>j</mi>\n    <mi>i</mi>\n  </msub>\n</math></span> at step <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>i</mi>\n</math></span> change to give a Fisher–Yates shuffle?</p>","back":"There are <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msup>\n    <mn>3</mn>\n    <mn>3</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>27</mn>\n</math></span> equally likely choice sequences. Every output probability is an integer multiple of <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>27</mn>\n</math></span>. Uniformity over six outputs would require <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>27</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>6</mn>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>4.5</mn>\n</math></span> choice sequences per output, impossible. Thus random swaps of this form are biased. In the forward Fisher–Yates version choose <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>j</mi>\n    <mi>i</mi>\n  </msub>\n</math></span> uniformly from <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo>\n  <mi>i</mi>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>i</mi>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mo>…</mo>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>3</mn>\n  <mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo>\n</math></span>. This fixes the next position from the remaining objects: any specified final permutation has probability <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>3</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mn>6</mn>\n</math></span>."}]